        <mxCell id="note_creds" value="&lt;b&gt;Credentials&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;All ten &amp;lt;service&amp;gt;_runtime passwords belong to the OpenBao database engine: one static role per runtime, rotated every 720 h by that cluster's vault_rotator (one openbao-db-config Job per cluster). External Secrets reads database/static-creds/&amp;lt;service&amp;gt;-runtime through the openbao-db store every 15 s into a Secret in the cluster namespace and in the service namespace; pods mount it and read DB_PASSWORD_FILE, and the DatabaseRoles carry no passwordSecret. OpenBao KV (store openbao, hourly) holds the migrators, db_authz, vault_rotator, Temporal and Keycloak, and the CDC logins: peerdb_&amp;lt;db&amp;gt;, analytics_heartbeat and peerdb_catalog. The CDC pooler (product-db-pooler-cdc, session mode, so PeerDB can open replication connections) looks logins up the same way; PeerDB reaches product-db only through it, and its catalog directly. pg_cron, inside product-db, writes the CDC heartbeats every 30 s. Neither application pooler holds a password: PgDog passes each login through to product-db, PgBouncer looks it up with auth_query over a client certificate. Every service, worker, migration and authz hop verifies the homelab-ca server certificate (verify-full); Keycloak, Temporal, OpenBao and pgroles do not yet (#1296, #1306). Backups authenticate to RustFS with pg-backup-rustfs-credentials." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1190" width="1950" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_dr" value="&lt;b&gt;Why the DR replica reads from RustFS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;product-db-replica never connects to the primary: it bootstraps from product-db's base backup and then replays its WAL archive from the bucket, so it survives the loss of the product-db pods. Its designated primary keeps its own archive and a daily backup in product-db-replica/ (7 d). Migrations always target the -rw service directly, never a pooler." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1282" width="1950" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
